CHANGELOG for raiapi/java/com/rai/raiapi
2005/Dec/23
  - Dictionary reload allowed (note that dictionary is in an undertermined stated during load operation so message dictionary operations may throw an error) 
  - RaiApi.haveDictionary is always reset at beginning of dictionary load 
  - Dictionary now checks for null session and throws exception 
  - Error codes now mostly same as c++ version 
2005/Oct/9
  - Fix to RaiSubscibe which was always doing both SNAP and SUB
  - Added TCP support
  - Remove dependency on RV libs (not tested) 
  - added test program subtest.java
2005/3/2  
  - Version chaged 1.3 Patch 4
  - Change logLevel to GetLogLevel,SetLevel
  - Add  GetHaveDictionary
  - Add  GetDictLoadInProgress
  - Change DictionaryTimeOutSeconds to Get/SetDictTimeoutSecs
  - Add trap for bad message in RaiDict OnMsg
2005/2/3
  - Version changed to 1.3 Patch 1
  - Fixed typo in RaiSubscribe.Destroy()

2005/1/30
  - Version change to 1.3 Patch 0
  - Changed addition of control fields to new methods:
      NewSASSMsg(), SASSInitalize(), NewRaiMsg, RaiMsgInitalize()
  - Added new RaiException constructor that takes reason, string and throwable

2005/1/27
  - Changed msgType test to use method to String.compareTo()
    test was failing on passed in String object
  - Added arguments msgType and logLevel to raipub example
  - Added enum for logLevel 0-Off, 1-Major, 2-Minor, 3-Debug, 4-Trace, 5-Full
  - classified debug messages according to logLevel

2005/1/25 
  - fix for subscriber delete
  - fix to correct publisher type not getting set correctly
2005/1/5 
  - event.receivedSubject fix to return message subject

2004/12/6
  - Improved RaiPublish constructor (this change is internal to API only) 
  - Now trapping error when form not set before publish (default is set to EQ and warning is printed)

2004/11/16
  - TCP support (including dictionary)
  - RV Dispatcher support added
  - dictionary now blocks
  - bug fixes
2004/11/01 Version 1.0 p2
  - added re-throw for caught errors
  - added error strings in RaiException
  - added cause for re-throws
  - added RaiEvent object to be returned in RaiCallback interface

2004/10/25 Version 1.0 p1
  - added internal method for RaiSession error strings
  - added multiple constructors for RaiExcetion

2004/10/18 Version 1.0
  - initial release 

